  "summary": "January 2026 reports apply self-supervised, contrastive and attention-based learning to purify, integrate and rank multi-omic features.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned models that operate directly on multi-omic or single-cell data to recover biological quantities or rank features. TwinPurify applies Barlow Twins self-supervised learning with adjacent-normal profiles as background to purify bulk tumor transcriptomes, and MONTE uses an empirical Bayes framework to estimate tumor purity and correct CpG methylation across 21 cancer types. Other items are predictive: a hybrid stacking-bagging ensemble fusing clinical, expression and CNV data reports ROC AUC 0.9355 on the METABRIC breast cancer cohort, and DeepGxP predicts protein and phosphoprotein abundance from transcriptomes. An unsupervised multivariate random forest with inverse minimal depth importance ranks cross-omics biomarkers and is reported to outperform sparse PLS and CCA under nonlinear conditions. Distinctively, TwinPurify and MONTE pair modeling with explicit correction for tumor purity and background tissue, while scMDCF and scPhase apply contrastive and attention-based architectures to single-cell data.",
